WEBVTT

00:24.520 --> 00:28.320
If we win, our dream ends.

00:29.900 --> 00:30.980
I don't want that.

00:31.900 --> 00:36.620
-I don't want to play like this.-
Ready, Rin?

00:39.990 --> 00:41.580
It ends with the first goal.

01:03.100 --> 01:04.310
Why?

01:05.060 --> 01:06.480
Bro!

01:07.350 --> 01:11.150
Rin, for four years while I was gone

01:15.280 --> 01:19.370
what were you doing here?

01:26.620 --> 01:30.130
BLUE LOCK RANKING

01:30.210 --> 01:33.800
BURATSUTA
JAPAN FOOTBALL ASSOCIATION

01:34.510 --> 01:37.380
<i>Is everything okay, Ego-kun?</i>

01:37.470 --> 01:39.470
BURATSUTA
JAPAN FOOTBALL ASSOCIATION

01:40.350 --> 01:42.260
<i>I'm grateful to you, you know.</i>

01:42.350 --> 01:45.940
<i>Thanks to Itoshi Sae's interest</i>
<i>in Blue Lock,</i>

01:46.020 --> 01:50.650
<i>the media is going crazy</i>
<i>and all tickets sold out instantly.</i>

01:50.730 --> 01:54.360
<i>A big match means big money.</i>

01:54.440 --> 01:58.570
<i>It will also help close your budget deficit.</i>

02:00.830 --> 02:02.540
Are you done spouting nonsense?

02:04.040 --> 02:06.750
<i>Are you serious?</i>

02:06.830 --> 02:09.630
<i>Do you really believe a team made up</i>
<i>of a bunch of forwards</i>

02:09.710 --> 02:15.510
<i>can actually beat an elite team</i>
<i>like Japan U-20?</i>

02:22.890 --> 02:24.090
I've said it before.

02:24.850 --> 02:29.350
Blue Lock was established to change Japanese football.

02:36.030 --> 02:38.190
ORIGINAL BY
MUNEYUKI KANESHIRO / YUSUKE NOMURA

04:12.120 --> 04:13.920
<i>Rough diamonds.</i>

04:14.000 --> 04:15.580
BLUE LOCK ADMINISTRATIVE DIRECTOR

04:15.670 --> 04:19.340
<i>Out of 300 high school forwards, you have managed</i>
<i>to survive a grueling elimination process.</i>

04:19.920 --> 04:21.970
<i>Now, only 35 of you remain,</i>

04:22.590 --> 04:26.890
<i>in pursuit of becoming the world's number one egoist.</i>

04:29.310 --> 04:31.770
<i>The match is in three weeks.</i>

04:31.850 --> 04:35.900
<i>You'll be playing against Japan U-20,</i>
<i>captained by Itoshi Sae.</i>

04:38.020 --> 04:42.070
If you win, you earn the right to represent Japan.

04:42.650 --> 04:43.780
<i>If you lose,</i>

04:45.200 --> 04:47.740
<i>Blue Lock is finished for good.</i>

04:47.830 --> 04:50.120
YOICHI ISAGI

04:50.200 --> 04:54.670
<i>A few months ago I was a complete nobody,</i>
<i>totally unknown.</i>

04:54.750 --> 04:55.790
ISAGI YOICHI-SAMA, YOU HAVE BEEN SELECTED TO BECOME A LICENSED ATHLETE

04:55.790 --> 04:58.710
<i>Then I was chosen for Blue Lock, learned about ego,</i>

04:58.790 --> 05:01.090
<i>and went through a lot to get here.</i>

05:02.590 --> 05:07.140
<i>If we win this, I can represent Japan.</i>

05:08.640 --> 05:10.310
<i>But if we lose,</i>

05:12.140 --> 05:16.480
<i>my football career will end along with Blue Lock.</i>

05:17.940 --> 05:19.610
<i>This match...</i>

05:19.690 --> 05:23.860
<i>This is my chance to completely change my life</i>
<i>with the skills I have.</i>

05:24.530 --> 05:26.240
Wait a minute.

05:26.320 --> 05:30.200
I get that this is our chance. But how are we going to form the teams?

05:30.780 --> 05:32.910
We're all forwards!

05:33.500 --> 05:38.250
Are you planning to stick some of us in midfield and defense?

05:38.330 --> 05:40.290
<i>Yes, naturally.</i>

05:40.380 --> 05:43.980
<i>We have no choice but to play with a makeshift</i>
<i>squad made up entirely of forwards.</i>

05:44.010 --> 05:46.130
Impossible! We can't win like that!

05:46.220 --> 05:49.300
We're up against real defenders!

05:49.390 --> 05:54.060
To be honest, I don't really care about that.

05:54.140 --> 05:56.350
Hey! It's not about whether you care or not-

05:56.440 --> 05:58.060
<i>Shut up, you chatterboxes.</i>

06:00.610 --> 06:04.990
I'm announcing the six players who will form the core of the team.

06:05.650 --> 06:06.650
These six,

06:06.650 --> 06:10.450
according to a comprehensive evaluation,
are Blue Lock's current Top 6.

06:11.580 --> 06:13.740
<i>Those whose name is called, step forward.</i>

06:14.830 --> 06:15.830
<i>First,</i>

06:17.870 --> 06:19.000
<i>Itoshi Rin.</i>

06:19.080 --> 06:22.040
RIN ITOSHI

06:22.630 --> 06:23.880
<i>Rin.</i>

06:23.960 --> 06:26.340
<i>I knew you'd be number one.</i>

06:28.090 --> 06:29.550
<i>Next, number 2,</i>

06:30.220 --> 06:31.600
<i>Shidou Ryusei.</i>

06:31.680 --> 06:32.720
Hell yeah.

06:32.720 --> 06:34.430
RYUSEI SHIDOU

06:36.060 --> 06:38.940
I didn't know you were that good.

06:42.230 --> 06:48.030
So you're No. 1 and I'm No. 2.
How exciting.

06:48.650 --> 06:50.160
<i>Four left.</i>

06:50.700 --> 06:53.530
<i>No. 3, Karasu Tabito.</i>

06:56.080 --> 06:58.040
You know why, dumbass.

06:58.120 --> 07:00.750
TABITO KARASU

07:01.330 --> 07:03.960
<i>No. 4, Otoya Eita.</i>

07:04.800 --> 07:05.880
EITA OTOYA

07:05.960 --> 07:07.130
Sup?

07:07.670 --> 07:10.550
<i>No. 5, Yukimiya Kenyu.</i>

07:10.630 --> 07:11.640
KENYU YUKIMIYA

07:11.640 --> 07:13.890
Yes, I'm honored.

07:14.680 --> 07:17.720
<i>I want to be that one person.</i>

07:18.390 --> 07:23.020
<i>I want to be in the main squad</i>
<i>formed by Blue Lock's Top 6.</i>

07:23.110 --> 07:25.360
<i>Finally, No. 6,</i>

07:27.570 --> 07:29.190
<i>Nagi Seishiro.</i>

07:29.280 --> 07:31.160
SEISHIRO NAGI

07:35.990 --> 07:36.990
<i>That's it.</i>

07:38.250 --> 07:39.160
Excuse me.

07:39.160 --> 07:41.790
<i>Ego-san, why am I fifth?</i>

07:42.500 --> 07:44.200
<i>What's the difference between me and first place?</i>

07:44.210 --> 07:45.920
<i>Very simple.</i>

07:46.000 --> 07:48.130
<i>Out of the 35 people,</i>

07:48.210 --> 07:51.720
<i>the only ones who managed to score</i>
<i>against the World Five</i>

07:52.590 --> 07:55.140
<i>were Itoshi Rin and Shidou Ryusei.</i>

07:55.220 --> 07:58.310
<i>The rest were ranked based on total goals</i>
<i>from the first selection</i>

07:58.390 --> 08:01.520
<i>and the evaluations of the World Five.</i>

08:01.600 --> 08:02.730
<i>And also,</i>

08:03.400 --> 08:05.190
<i>according to my own whims.</i>

08:05.270 --> 08:07.920
<i>Are you satisfied, Mr. Mild-Mannered</i>
<i>Glasses-Wearing Model?</i>

08:07.940 --> 08:09.150
Yes.

08:09.230 --> 08:11.780
-Thank you very much.
-That guy's a model?

08:11.860 --> 08:13.320
He must be joking.

08:14.450 --> 08:17.870
<i>Also, the next selection now begins.</i>

08:18.660 --> 08:22.790
<i>First, these six will be divided into three teams</i>
<i>according to their rankings.</i>

08:25.130 --> 08:30.460
<i>The remaining 29 players must decide which duo</i>
<i>they will team up with.</i>

08:30.550 --> 08:36.890
<i>You'll form five-man teams by adding three people</i>
<i>to each team.</i>

08:36.970 --> 08:39.600
<i>Each team will play a five-on-five match.</i>

08:40.640 --> 08:41.680
<i>I see.</i>

08:42.310 --> 08:47.730
<i>They're looking for people who fit the attacking style</i>
<i>of the Top 6.</i>

08:48.320 --> 08:54.530
<i>The 29 people outside the Top 6 will only get</i>
<i>one chance to play.</i>

08:54.610 --> 08:55.510
<i>These pairings</i>

08:56.490 --> 09:02.160
<i>will determine who makes it to the match</i>
<i>against Japan U-20.</i>

09:02.250 --> 09:05.580
Just one chance to prove ourselves?

09:05.670 --> 09:08.000
Sounds pretty professional.

09:08.590 --> 09:10.460
Bring it on!

09:10.550 --> 09:15.590
<i>Due to the number of players, one team</i>
<i>will play twice.</i>

09:15.680 --> 09:19.180
<i>That team will include No. 7.</i>

09:20.720 --> 09:24.100
<i>Bachira Meguru. You'll be on that team.</i>

09:25.270 --> 09:27.060
Okay, sir.

09:27.650 --> 09:30.520
<i>Damn it. We've been playing together since the start,</i>

09:31.280 --> 09:33.650
<i>and yet they're all better than me?</i>

09:34.280 --> 09:38.410
<i>The Top 6 will be taken to another room.</i>

09:42.540 --> 09:45.540
<i>These rankings only show where you currently stand.</i>

09:45.620 --> 09:49.630
<i>Even someone in the Top 6 can lose their spot</i>
<i>if they fail the selection.</i>

09:49.710 --> 09:51.750
<i>Don't forget that.</i>

09:54.510 --> 09:58.300
<i>I have a message for the remaining 29.</i>

09:58.390 --> 10:02.560
<i>The key to passing the selection is</i>
<i>'assertiveness and teamwork'.</i>

10:03.520 --> 10:07.310
<i>Against the Top 6, with your masterful skills</i>
<i>and goal-scoring ability,</i>

10:07.390 --> 10:12.980
<i>prove yourself and become one of them</i>
<i>as a unique individual.</i>

10:13.070 --> 10:14.440
<i>Lastly,</i>

10:17.280 --> 10:18.910
<i>sabotage them!</i>

10:19.570 --> 10:24.910
<i>For you, the Top 6 are not teammates</i>
<i>you're going to play alongside.</i>

10:25.540 --> 10:28.420
<i>They are merely obstacles.</i>
<i>Therefore, dominate them.</i>

10:29.710 --> 10:32.040
<i>For the future I dream of,</i>
<i>I have to play in that match.</i>

10:32.130 --> 10:34.500
<i>To do that, I need to get on a good team.</i>

10:35.130 --> 10:36.260
DOMINATION

10:36.340 --> 10:37.550
<i>Now, choose.</i>

10:39.050 --> 10:43.350
<i>Carefully select the best teammates</i>
<i>who will determine your future and destiny.</i>

10:49.190 --> 10:51.730
3RD SELECTION
GRAND DINING HALL

10:51.810 --> 10:53.150
Hey.

10:53.770 --> 10:54.780
Igaguri.

10:54.860 --> 10:57.240
Did you take every plate?

10:57.320 --> 11:01.530
The buffet's only open tonight,
I have to make the most of it.

11:01.620 --> 11:03.000
Don't underestimate my desires!

11:03.030 --> 11:05.240
Give me one of your desires.

11:06.370 --> 11:08.250
Go get your own!

11:09.160 --> 11:12.630
Desires taste great with tartar sauce.

11:12.700 --> 11:14.100
A meal where desires unite!

11:14.120 --> 11:16.710
Gagamaru, use chopsticks. Here, take these.

11:16.710 --> 11:18.420
Shut up and eat, idiots!

11:19.470 --> 11:20.930
Anyway.

11:21.010 --> 11:26.470
I guess the old Team Z couldn't get back together.

11:26.560 --> 11:30.440
You're right. I'm sad Naruhaya isn't here.

11:30.520 --> 11:36.270
Plus Traitor Kuon,
Playboy Imamura, Keeper Lemon...

11:38.440 --> 11:39.480
And, Kunigami.

11:42.700 --> 11:47.580
To be honest, I never thought Kunigami would get eliminated.

11:47.660 --> 11:49.010
I mean, he's so good.

11:51.000 --> 11:53.170
Shidou kicked him out.

11:53.790 --> 11:56.210
But this is Blue Lock.

11:56.290 --> 11:57.800
Chigiri.

11:58.380 --> 12:03.430
If we lose to the U-20s anyway, everything will have been for nothing.

12:03.510 --> 12:06.810
We don't have time to worry about the others.

12:06.890 --> 12:07.970
True.

12:08.720 --> 12:12.440
Have you chosen who you're going to team up with?

12:12.520 --> 12:13.560
JINGO RAICHI
CIRCLE THE TEAM YOU'VE CHOSEN

12:13.560 --> 12:15.860
I'm picking Team A.

12:15.940 --> 12:18.280
I teamed up with Shidou before.

12:18.360 --> 12:20.610
I think either B or C.

12:20.690 --> 12:22.450
Just a feeling.

12:23.030 --> 12:25.070
I'll decide with a stair lottery.

12:25.160 --> 12:27.530
Besides, I need to play two matches.

12:27.620 --> 12:29.240
Right.

12:29.330 --> 12:32.870
So, are you the most successful guy from the old Team Z?

12:32.960 --> 12:34.620
That bothers me.

12:34.710 --> 12:36.750
I'm an egoist!

12:36.840 --> 12:38.210
What about you, Chigiri?

12:38.300 --> 12:40.510
I haven't decided yet. You, Isagi?

12:41.760 --> 12:44.010
I...

12:44.090 --> 12:45.510
Either A or C, right?

12:45.590 --> 12:47.800
Either Rin-chan or Nagi.

12:47.890 --> 12:49.560
Actually, yeah.

12:49.640 --> 12:51.220
How did you know?

12:52.270 --> 12:54.640
If you want a chemical reaction with your weapon,

12:54.730 --> 12:58.320
<i>you can achieve that with Nagi on Team C.</i>

12:58.400 --> 13:02.530
<i>But if you want to bet on your undiscovered</i>
<i>unknown potential,</i>

13:02.610 --> 13:04.650
<i>Team A with Rin-chan.</i>

13:04.740 --> 13:05.910
Right?

13:06.450 --> 13:07.450
Yeah.

13:08.580 --> 13:11.410
<i>'Assertiveness and teamwork,' huh.</i>

13:12.450 --> 13:16.330
<i>Who is the best option for me to team up with?</i>

13:17.250 --> 13:20.250
TOP 6
VIP ROOM

13:23.800 --> 13:26.930
I'm Yukimiya Kenyu. Nice to meet you.

13:27.970 --> 13:30.930
Nagi Seishiro. Nice to meet you too, Mr. Four Eyes.

13:31.720 --> 13:35.520
I'm excited to see who will team up with us.

13:39.690 --> 13:42.230
Let's get along, 'No. 1'.

13:43.820 --> 13:47.070
Don't ignore me. We're teammates now.

13:48.660 --> 13:50.780
Do you like explosions?

13:51.450 --> 13:52.700
Not interested.

13:52.790 --> 13:54.790
Get lost, Antenna Head.

14:00.420 --> 14:02.210
Nice. Come on then.

14:03.960 --> 14:05.670
Should we stop them?

14:05.760 --> 14:07.090
Let them go.

14:07.180 --> 14:09.980
If they kill each other, it's to our advantage.

14:10.350 --> 14:12.600
Headbutt.

14:12.680 --> 14:14.020
Bastard.

14:14.100 --> 14:17.270
Don't get in the way of my play or I'll kill you.

14:17.350 --> 14:20.190
That has nothing to do with football.

14:20.270 --> 14:22.650
It's purely a biological need!

14:23.280 --> 14:26.190
<i>Alright, stop the idiocy.</i>

14:28.320 --> 14:29.820
Get a hold of yourselves a little.

14:31.660 --> 14:34.790
<i>I have to say, you are the best of Blue Lock.</i>

14:35.410 --> 14:38.790
<i>Each team is made up of the best forward duos</i>

14:38.870 --> 14:41.630
<i>capable of playing an experimental and super-offensive style.</i>

14:42.250 --> 14:45.880
<i>Show me new attacking patterns that you couldn't create alone.</i>

14:45.960 --> 14:48.460
<i>To become the world's best,</i>

14:48.500 --> 14:50.500
<i>think of the other player as a tool.</i>

14:51.140 --> 14:55.430
<i>And no matter what,</i>

14:55.520 --> 14:57.980
<i>don't let anyone steal your spot in the Top 6.</i>

14:58.560 --> 15:01.690
<i>You stand at the top of Blue Lock.</i>

15:02.980 --> 15:05.110
Remember this:

15:05.190 --> 15:08.900
the football you create will be the sword that cuts through Japanese football.

15:16.450 --> 15:19.710
I want to see you competing with yourselves.

15:23.130 --> 15:27.210
<i>First, let's think about what we're being tested on in this selection.</i>

15:28.720 --> 15:32.510
<i>When he said teamwork, did he mean we need</i>
<i>to adapt to the Top 6?</i>

15:33.140 --> 15:37.600
<i>And then he said 'assertiveness'.</i>
<i>So, not to be crushed under them?</i>

15:38.180 --> 15:42.940
<i>So I have to figure out what he means and show</i>
<i>myself in just one match?</i>

15:43.020 --> 15:46.020
<i>This selection is impossible.</i>

15:46.110 --> 15:48.610
I can't wrap my head around it!

15:48.690 --> 15:49.510
Don't stress.

15:49.610 --> 15:52.990
Not confident in yourself? Sucks.

15:53.620 --> 15:55.620
You decided, Barou?

15:55.700 --> 15:58.620
Doesn't matter much, but Team C with Mr. Hassle.

15:58.700 --> 16:02.170
Playing with familiar faces won't help me develop

16:02.250 --> 16:05.920
and wherever I am, I'll be the only king.

16:06.500 --> 16:07.800
That's all.

16:08.380 --> 16:11.130
Wow. That's so typical of you.

16:11.220 --> 16:15.550
Anyway, why aren't you in the Top 6, Isagi?

16:15.640 --> 16:16.670
What?

16:17.930 --> 16:19.140
It drives me crazy.

16:19.810 --> 16:22.190
I want to crush you.

16:22.810 --> 16:26.440
Don't let yourself be crushed in a place like this, donkey.

16:26.520 --> 16:29.230
You're right. I'm sorry.

16:33.240 --> 16:36.700
Isagi-kun, I'm borrowing your face wash.

16:36.780 --> 16:38.240
What? Niko.

16:39.490 --> 16:43.080
Seems like you haven't picked a team yet.

16:43.160 --> 16:45.420
Right.

16:47.000 --> 16:51.130
It's like Ego-san is trying to stoke our competitive spirit,

16:51.210 --> 16:54.680
but I think the real test is whether we can fit in with the Top 6.

16:55.260 --> 16:56.930
Adapting to them.

16:57.010 --> 16:58.310
Have you decided, Niko?

16:59.140 --> 17:03.560
I'm fine with anyone who lets me play my own style.

17:03.640 --> 17:06.100
I'm tired of always being in the background.

17:07.110 --> 17:10.780
You're the one who taught me that the lead role is something to be stolen.

17:12.860 --> 17:15.990
<i>Someone who lets you be the lead…</i>

17:21.040 --> 17:22.160
Hey, Isagi-kun.

17:22.250 --> 17:23.410
Yes?

17:23.500 --> 17:25.210
Are you going to go out now?

17:25.790 --> 17:28.500
I don't want anyone to see me washing my forehead.

17:28.590 --> 17:30.250
What? Sorry.

17:30.340 --> 17:32.380
<i>Why would he be embarrassed about that?</i>

17:38.970 --> 17:43.850
<i>I know proving myself</i>
<i>while on the same team as Rin won't be easy.</i>

17:43.930 --> 17:47.600
<i>I might get eliminated without doing anything.</i>

17:48.230 --> 17:50.680
<i>Which means the person I should team up with...</i>

17:53.610 --> 17:55.860
Not easy to decide, is it?

17:55.950 --> 17:56.980
Reo.

17:58.240 --> 17:59.450
Same here.

18:00.740 --> 18:03.240
I thought your only option would be Nagi's team.

18:04.450 --> 18:07.750
Funny coming from the person who drove a wedge between Nagi and me.

18:07.830 --> 18:09.500
Sorry.

18:10.790 --> 18:14.460
That was my plan, but I'm not so sure anymore.

18:15.420 --> 18:16.420
Why's that?

18:17.260 --> 18:22.680
I'll tell you, in the second selection he chose you over me,

18:23.350 --> 18:27.640
and my desire for revenge brought me this far.

18:29.600 --> 18:34.320
But watching him rise to the Top 6

18:34.400 --> 18:37.240
and comparing myself to him objectively,

18:37.990 --> 18:41.320
he's reaching a level I can't catch up to.

18:42.330 --> 18:44.620
Plus, I don't have the courage to play alongside him.

18:46.500 --> 18:49.960
But if I miss this chance, I might not get another.

18:51.500 --> 18:56.550
Also, if I show him my weakness, he could pull even further ahead.

19:00.590 --> 19:03.010
Right now, I don't know what to do.

19:05.930 --> 19:07.230
Same, Reo.

19:08.520 --> 19:09.940
You're right.

19:10.560 --> 19:15.690
If we don't team up now, he might become someone we can never catch.

19:17.940 --> 19:20.110
That's something I don't want to regret.

19:21.110 --> 19:23.620
Okay. Thanks, Reo.

19:23.700 --> 19:25.900
Thank you very much, I've got my head straight now.

19:26.120 --> 19:29.000
I'm sure it's not about what the right path is.

19:29.580 --> 19:33.880
What matters is making your own choice into the right path.

19:35.420 --> 19:40.680
I'll prove that the path I chose wasn't a mistake!

19:44.050 --> 19:46.060
<i>Voting is over.</i>

19:46.140 --> 19:47.770
<i>The final selection begins.</i>

19:48.930 --> 19:52.810
<i>Put on your jerseys immediately and</i>
<i>gather in the hall right away.</i>

19:55.860 --> 19:57.110
FINAL SELECTION
ASSEMBLY AREA

19:57.190 --> 20:00.740
<i>I am announcing the teams.</i>

20:01.610 --> 20:06.120
<i>So the final selection before the match</i>
<i>against Japan U-20 is starting.</i>

20:06.200 --> 20:09.250
<i>Who makes Blue Lock 11 will be decided here.</i>

20:09.830 --> 20:11.830
<i>The team I chose...</i>

20:11.920 --> 20:13.330
12 PLAYERS

20:13.420 --> 20:15.920
<i>The person I want to play with,</i>

20:17.380 --> 20:19.090
<i>is you, Rin.</i>

20:21.550 --> 20:24.800
<i>Bachira chose Team A as well.</i>

20:24.890 --> 20:26.890
3RD FINAL SELECTION TRIALS

20:26.970 --> 20:30.680
<i>Barou, Raichi, Niko, and Chigiri are</i>
<i>on the same team.</i>

20:32.730 --> 20:35.810
<i>On Nagi's team,</i>
<i>I see Gagamaru and Zantetsu.</i>

20:35.900 --> 20:36.900
9 PLAYERS

20:36.980 --> 20:38.860
<i>Reo is on C as well.</i>

20:39.530 --> 20:43.200
<i>So you chose Nagi's team.</i>

20:44.450 --> 20:46.570
<i>The key to passing the selection</i>

20:46.660 --> 20:49.120
<i>is 'assertiveness and teamwork'.</i>

20:50.910 --> 20:56.500
<i>What matters is how I get involved</i>
<i>in the flow of the game and make my mark.</i>

20:57.880 --> 21:03.300
<i>After this match comes Japan U-20.</i>

21:08.260 --> 21:10.100
Hoicchan.

21:10.180 --> 21:11.180
JAPAN FOOTBALL ASSOCIATION SPECIAL ADVISOR

21:11.180 --> 21:13.430
You understand, don't you?

21:14.060 --> 21:14.960
Yes.

21:14.980 --> 21:15.850
U-20 MANAGER
SEIJI HOICHI

21:15.940 --> 21:18.610
Sacrifice everything for Japanese football.

21:23.740 --> 21:24.860
Crush them.

21:24.950 --> 21:27.450
They must be crushed.

21:27.530 --> 21:31.790
We can't let Japanese football fall into the hands of a few lunatics.

21:31.870 --> 21:35.960
Please don't worry. They're just idealistic people.

21:36.040 --> 21:41.380
There's no one else who can be on Japan U-20 but us.

21:46.720 --> 21:52.100
There's our 'Earless Hoichi', he listens to no one but the JFU.

21:52.180 --> 21:55.890
I got mocked online because of that nickname, please stop.

21:58.600 --> 22:01.820
Well, you heard everything. I'm counting on you, captain.

22:02.400 --> 22:03.610
Got it.

22:03.690 --> 22:08.240
We accept Blue Lock.

22:09.990 --> 22:13.330
<i>We'll win! And I'll prove it.</i>

22:13.410 --> 22:17.960
<i>I will become the world's number one forward.</i>

23:49.970 --> 23:52.970
<i>Blue Lock Extras.</i>

23:53.050 --> 23:55.970
TOP 6'S ROOMS

23:56.060 --> 23:56.970
EGO JINPACHI

23:56.970 --> 24:00.430
Now prepare for the trials, Top 6.

24:03.060 --> 24:04.770
-Okay.
-So there are two triple rooms.

24:04.770 --> 24:05.610
YUKIMIYA KENYU
KARASU TABITO

24:05.690 --> 24:08.110
We need to split into two groups.

24:08.190 --> 24:09.490
How do you want to do it?

24:09.570 --> 24:12.030
I'll stay in this room alone.

24:12.110 --> 24:13.780
The five of you stay in the other one.

24:13.870 --> 24:15.160
What are you saying?

24:15.240 --> 24:16.990
No way. Not possible.

24:17.080 --> 24:18.080
NAGI SEISHIRO

24:18.160 --> 24:20.580
Then let's make teams with rock-paper-scissors.

24:20.660 --> 24:23.000
We'll just split into two groups.

24:23.080 --> 24:25.420
Come on, come on. I'm not that eager.

24:25.500 --> 24:28.500
How about the loser of rock-paper-scissors sleeps outside?

24:28.550 --> 24:31.510
I like that. Ego-ego rock-paper-scissors.

24:32.180 --> 24:34.180
What? Sounds bothersome.

24:34.260 --> 24:36.850
-No way! It's super exciting!
-Hey.

24:36.930 --> 24:38.810
-Ego-ego rock-paper-scissors. Rock.
-Hey.

24:38.890 --> 24:40.890
-Paper!
-Yeah, super exciting.

24:40.980 --> 24:42.480
-Rock-paper-scissors.
-Scissors!

24:43.600 --> 24:47.730
Let's all say who we want to share a room with.

24:47.820 --> 24:51.220
We'll arrange the split so we won't end up staying with them.

24:51.860 --> 24:53.490
-Okay
-Works.

24:53.570 --> 24:55.280
Okay. Let's do it.

24:55.360 --> 24:57.280
Alright then. Ready and...

25:02.580 --> 25:04.750
Fine, I'll take one room for myself.

25:04.830 --> 25:07.590
No, forget it. Let's change the rule.

25:09.630 --> 25:12.550
Then I'll stay with Rin-kun.

25:12.630 --> 25:16.730
Nagi-kun, I want to have a strategy talk with you. How about staying with us?

25:17.090 --> 25:19.100
What? Okay, I guess.

25:19.890 --> 25:22.270
More discussion is a hassle,

25:22.350 --> 25:24.550
I hope we'll be good roommates, Mr. Four Eyes.

25:25.060 --> 25:26.690
And you too, Monster.

25:27.690 --> 25:28.810
Makes no difference to me.

25:28.900 --> 25:31.690
YUKIMIYA, NAGI, AND RIN
ARE STAYING IN THE SAME ROOM!

25:33.780 --> 25:35.950
Nice to stay in the same room as you, Hedgehog Head.

25:36.030 --> 25:37.660
Speak for yourself.

25:37.740 --> 25:39.870
Look, I'm a hedgehog head too.

25:39.950 --> 25:43.080
OTOYA, KARASU, AND SHIDOU
ARE STAYING IN THE SAME ROOM!